                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2]Cute Adventure/Puzzle Game but too short[/h2]\r\n\r\nI played through Jacob Jones Episodes 1 and 2 last year and it was actually quite fun to play although it is way too short. Too bad they didn't make any more episodes.\r\n\r\nThe Jacob Jones games are similar to the older Professor Layton series. It contains some brain teasers and I didn't find them too challenging.\r\n\r\nThe art design is cute and still holds up well today. Cartoonish graphics never get old to me. The voice acting is well done and the story is simple.\r\n\r\nThe collection achievements were mostly easy to get, took some backtracking and I almost didn't find the final Gnatnobbler. Love that name lol. As for the merit achievements, that was tricky. Finishing that one ended up with me resorting to guides to complete it.\r\n\r\nMy inner child very much enjoyed playing the Jacob Jones episodes. I recommend these episodes if you're looking for short games to 100 percent.\r\n\r\n[h2]7/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h3][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h3]",
